---

<Layout title="Synapse Engine | Open-source GPU-driven engine for graphics research and education">

    <!-- ============================== HERO (full screen) ============================== -->
    <section class="relative isolate overflow-hidden min-h-[calc(100svh-4rem)] flex flex-col">
        <div class="absolute inset-0 -z-10 bg-[url('/Images/Home/Home.png')] bg-cover bg-center opacity-100 dark:opacity-100"></div>
        <div class="absolute inset-0 -z-10 bg-gradient-to-b from-bg/60 via-bg/80 to-bg"></div>

        <div class="wrap flex-1 flex flex-col items-center justify-center text-center py-20">
            <p class="eyebrow mb-8">Open source · C++23 · Vulkan 1.4</p>
            <h1 class="max-w-5xl text-[2.75rem] leading-[1.04] sm:text-6xl md:text-7xl lg:text-[5.5rem] font-semibold tracking-[-0.035em]">
                A modern game engine architecture, built for graphics research.
            </h1>
            <p class="lead mt-8 max-w-2xl">
                Synapse Engine is an open-source, fully GPU-driven game engine designed for university research groups,
                PhD students and anyone who wants to understand how a state-of-the-art renderer is put together.
            </p>
            <div class="mt-10 flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-3">
                <a href="https://github.com/TamasPetii/SynapseEngine" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn-primary">
                    <svg class="h-4 w-4" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor"><path d="M12 0c-6.626 0-12 5.373-12 12 0 5.302 3.438 9.8 8.207 11.387.599.111.793-.261.793-.577v-2.234c-3.338.726-4.033-1.416-4.033-1.416-.546-1.387-1.333-1.756-1.333-1.756-1.089-.745.083-.729.083-.729 1.205.084 1.839 1.237 1.839 1.237 1.07 1.834 2.807 1.304 3.492.997.107-.775.418-1.305.762-1.604-2.665-.305-5.467-1.334-5.467-5.931 0-1.311.469-2.381 1.236-3.221-.124-.303-.535-1.524.117-3.176 0 0 1.008-.322 3.301 1.23.957-.266 1.983-.399 3.003-.404 1.02.005 2.047.138 3.006.404 2.291-1.552 3.297-1.23 3.297-1.23.653 1.653.242 2.874.118 3.176.77.84 1.235 1.911 1.235 3.221 0 4.609-2.807 5.624-5.479 5.921.43.372.823 1.102.823 2.222v3.293c0 .319.192.694.801.576 4.765-1.589 8.199-6.086 8.199-11.386 0-6.627-5.373-12-12-12z"/></svg>
                    Source code
                </a>
                <a href={DHAC_TALK} target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn-secondary bg-bg/60 backdrop-blur-sm">Dual-HiZ talk</a>
                <a href={DEEP_DIVE} target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn-secondary bg-bg/60 backdrop-blur-sm">
                    Technical deep dive <span class="font-mono text-xs text-faint">250 p</span>
                </a>
            </div>
        </div>

        <a href="#why" class="mx-auto pb-8 flex flex-col items-center gap-1.5 text-xs text-faint hover:text-fg transition-colors">
            Scroll
            <svg class="h-4 w-4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M12 5v14m0 0-6-6m6 6 6-6"/></svg>
        </a>
    </section>

    <!-- ============================== THE GAP + WHO IT'S FOR ============================== -->
    <section id="why" class="border-y border-line bg-surface scroll-mt-16">
        <div class="wrap py-20 md:py-28">
            <p class="eyebrow mb-4">Why Synapse exists</p>
            <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight leading-[1.15]">The gap between AAA engines and university research.</h2>

            <div class="mt-10 grid gap-x-12 gap-y-5 md:grid-cols-2 body text-[17px]">
                <p>
                    Unreal and Unity are built to ship games. Their codebases have grown for decades, so isolating one algorithm
                    or measuring it fairly is hard work, even when the source is open.
                </p>
                <p>
                    Research frameworks like NVIDIA Falcor are great for prototyping a single rendering pass, but they don't
                    model a full modern engine. So most university groups end up maintaining a small framework of their own.
                </p>
            </div>
            <p class="mt-8 text-xl font-medium text-fg">Synapse Engine is built to fill that gap.</p>

            <!-- Comparison table -->
            <div class="mt-12 rounded-lg border border-line bg-bg">
                <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-center justify-between gap-4 px-6 pt-6 pb-4">
                    <h3 class="text-base font-semibold">How existing engines fit research use</h3>
                    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-4 text-xs text-muted">
                        <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5"><span class="mark mark-yes">✓</span> Yes</span>
                        <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5"><span class="mark mark-part">∼</span> Partly</span>
                        <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5"><span class="mark mark-no">×</span> No</span>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="overflow-x-auto">
                    <table class="w-full min-w-[760px] text-sm border-collapse">
                        <thead>
                            <tr class="border-y border-line">
                                <th class="py-3 pl-6 pr-4 text-left text-xs font-medium text-muted w-[22%]">Engine</th>
                                {landscapeCols.map((c) => (
                                    <th class="py-3 px-2 text-center text-xs font-medium text-muted leading-snug">{c}</th>
                                ))}
                            </tr>
                        </thead>
                        <tbody>
                            {landscape.map((row) => (
                                <tr class="border-b border-line">
