            <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight leading-[1.15]">GPU-built Morton chunk hierarchy</h2>

            <div class="mt-10 grid gap-x-12 gap-y-5 md:grid-cols-2 body text-[17px]">
                <p>
                    With millions of static objects, even launching the culling threads becomes measurable. So for static
                    geometry the engine adds one more level above the models.
                </p>
                <p>
                    The GPU computes a Morton code for every static entity, sorts them with a radix sort and groups them into
                    chunks of 32 nearby models. One rejected chunk removes 32 models at once. Building it on the GPU takes
                    about 3 ms instead of 130 ms on the CPU.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="mt-14 grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-2">
                <Figure src={`${IMG}/Morton_Outside.png`} crop alt="Morton chunks seen from outside">Chunk bounds seen from outside.</Figure>
